WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:11.760
Hey youtubers it’s charlie, this is the
sherlock empty hearse breakdown that I’ve

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.750
been promising for the last couple of days.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:19.230
What i’ll do is go through the episode and
include as many references as possible and

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.970
interesting facts about the story and the
production.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:24.590
So it will be a little different than one
of my easter egg videos.

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.980
There’s actually a bunch of stuff going
on this weekend between new sherlock and anime

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.450
club so if you’re finding me for the first
time be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.200
Since this video conveys so many details about
the plot and details of the story.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.770
This is your super spoiler warning.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.070
The episode is so long and there are so many
details, this video will just focus on the

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:43.070
parts of itI think are the most important.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.130
Here we go let’s blow the doors of the empty
hearse.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:49.000
Number 1 - The title is a reference to the
conan doyle story the empty house.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.900
Both this episode and that book brought the
character back from the dead so to speak.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.540
Doyle killed the character in his novel The
Final Problem.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:59.460
The character was so popular that fans and
his publisher compelled him to bring the character

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:00.460
back.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.500
Which led to The adventures of the empty house.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.900
So if anyone didn’t like that there was
so much fan service in episode 1, remember

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:09.950
that conan doyle’s novel empty house was
essentially written as fan service.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.299
Number 2 - Sherlock Lives Theories.

00:01:12.299 --> 00:01:16.319
We don’t learn what we’re seeing is Anderson’s
theory until the last frame cuts after this

00:01:16.319 --> 00:01:17.319
first scenario.

00:01:17.319 --> 00:01:19.640
Let me know below in the comments how long
it took you to figure out.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:25.310
I didn’t realize until the Molly Kiss, but
the weird dance track made me suspicious.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.310
Derren Brown is actually a famous real life
hypnotist.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:32.030
Sherlock tells watson later that there were
13 possibilities of how he could survive.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:36.200
There’s a big debate going on in the fandom
as to whether he meant 13 ways he could have

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.459
faked his death or 13 ways he could have escaped
moriarty.

00:01:40.459 --> 00:01:45.249
Most presume that he never suspected moriarty
would be so committed to his plan that he’d

00:01:45.249 --> 00:01:47.810
kill himself to force sherlock’s hand.

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.729
All of the scenarios were filmed in broad
daylight with a full crowd of reporters and

00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:52.939
people watching.

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:56.649
No one leaked any of the information, but
there were a few pictures that made it to

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:57.649
tumblr.

00:01:57.649 --> 00:01:59.729
3 - Moriarty Returns.

00:01:59.729 --> 00:02:03.709
Andrew Scott who plays moriarty appears in
all of the rooftop scenarios.

00:02:03.709 --> 00:02:06.049
All those scenes were filmed during series
3 production.

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:07.929
Meaning he came back on set.

00:02:07.929 --> 00:02:11.950
Early on people leaked that he would be part
of the new episodes misleading people into

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.700
thinking he didn’t die on the rooftop.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.640
Later we learned that he did in fact die from
the gunshot, people keep asking me what happened

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:19.950
to his body.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:23.730
Because sherlock and mycroft were one step
ahead of moriarty the whole time.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:27.430
They had a government crew ready to take the
body into custody.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.890
4 - Mycroft knew the whole time.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:34.091
After lestrad calls anderson on his crackpot
theory the press montage let’s us know that

00:02:34.091 --> 00:02:37.720
everyone ended up learning the real truth
about what moriarty did to sherlock.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:42.550
Because both sherlock and mycroft were one
step ahead, they allowed moriarty to discredit

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:43.550
sherlock.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:47.700
So once sherlock got rid of moriarty’s terror
network there was no more reason to keep up

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.700
the deception.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.630
Which is why the press are just now figuring
out the truth.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.020
5 - Mustache watch begins.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:57.740
We see watson with the caterpiller on his
lip and mary morstan.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.950
Freeman was actually on loan to steven moffat
and mark gatiss for 6 weeks to film the first

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.100
two episodes from peter jackson.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:07.190
They had to film both empty hearse and episode
2 sign of three while production of the hobbit

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:08.190
trilogy was still happening.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:11.670
So peter jackson rearranged freeman’s shooting
schedule to allow him to return to england

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.350
to film with the sherlock team briefly.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.440
So his mustache was fake the whole time.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.320
It’s kind of a sign that he’s let himself
go.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:23.500
He explains to mrs hudson that he never called
her because he let a lot of things slide.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.350
Including shaving his upper lip..

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.340
6 - Mary Morstan.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.460
Mary is played by amanda abbington, martin
freeman’s real life partner.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:33.630
And if you haven’t seen them together, they’re
pretty adorable.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:36.090
7 - Sherlock on the cross.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:40.600
The russian base sherlock got caught breaking
into was the last place he went to dismantle

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:41.600
moriarty’s terror cell.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:42.600
That’s why he was there.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.090
As a character he’s kind of regressed emotionally
because he’s been on his own for the past

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.090
two years.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.090
The interesting thing is that the whole time
he carried watson around in his head.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.090
That’s why you catch him talking to an imaginary
watson when he’s with molly later.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.090
He probably did that all the time over the
past two years.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.090
So in a way, even though sherlock left watson,
watson never left sherlock.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:51.090
8 - Mycroft in the field.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:52.090
The mycroft character in the books is much
more isolated than mark gatiss’ version.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:57.470
So even though he complains it’s actually
a huge deal that mycroft came out to help

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.470
sherlock.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.660
You learn later that mycroft is actually smarter
than sherlock. and that when they were growing

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:06.850
up sherlock though he was stupid by comparison
until they met other children and he realized

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.590
that he and mycroft were different.

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:11.720
Think of mycroft and sherlock on a sliding
scale of weirdness and intellect.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:12.720
The smarter they get the more isolated they
become socially.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:16.000
So sherlock is brilliant and can co-exist
with other humans.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.880
Mycroft is a genius and can’t stand people.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:20.519
9 - back to london.

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:23.730
The terror plot that brings sherlock back
to london got a lot of complaints from fans

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.730
of the novel series.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:28.780
Mark Gatiss used the sebastian moran character
as part of the tube bomb plot and in the episode

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:29.780
the character is kind of wasted.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:30.870
He just sits on the bed and pushes a button.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.350
In the novels, Sebastian moran is like an
evil version of watson.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:39.080
they both served in the military but sebastian
met moriarty instead of meeting sherlock.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:43.910
So imagine what watson would have become after
leaving afghanistan if he had met moriarty

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:44.910
instead of sherlock.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:51.520
Most of the complaints about the moran character
are that in the novels he and moriarty have

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.380
this really interesting relationship that
you never see play out on screen.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:59.310
A lot of people confused molly’s fiancee
with the sniper from rikenback fall.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:05.980
That sniper was moran and in this episode
moran is the government official that sets

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:06.980
off the bomb.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:08.230
Sherlock calls Moran as the head rat.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:12.000
It’s a reference to a holmes adventure that
was talked about but never happened in the

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.389
books, called the giant rat of sumatra.

00:05:14.389 --> 00:05:19.300
It’s also a street near bull and bush in
west hampshead for which platforms and staircases

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.350
were built but no above ground entry.

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:23.290
10 - The tube is wonky.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:28.060
A lot of people noticed that the plotting
and the maps of the london tube were all wrong.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.970
This was on purpose.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:34.060
The maps of the tube are heavily copyrighted
and no one is ever allowed to use them in

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.060
film or tv.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.060
So they had to make their own maps that could
look anything like the real ones.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.530
11 - Mustache references.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:42.590
I know I promised to count all the mustache
jokes.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:48.110
3, 3,7,6

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:52.460
12 - Johnlock for the win.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:54.860
When watson tells mrs hudon that he’s getting
engaged mrs hudson is generally surprised

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:55.860
that it’s to a woman.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.310
In my opinion she genuinely thought that he
and sherlock were a couple the whole time

00:05:58.310 --> 00:05:59.310
they were together.

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:00.620
Which is hilarious.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:05.220
It also pays homage to the subtext the fandom
has always read into the characters.

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:07.320
13 - The upturned collar.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.600
The first time sherlock puts the jacket back
on is the first time the game is on theme

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.600
stirs.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:15.270
It doesn’t play in full until he re-enters
baker street.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:19.880
To the screams of mrs hudson.
14 - The reunion.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:24.290
Sherlock disguises himself trying to find
a clever way to let watson know he’s alive.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:27.670
This is a joke about the character’s master
of disguise persona.

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:31.200
The real joke is that watson doesn’t even
notice him at first.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.770
The three diamonds on watson’s engagement
ring are a subtle visual reference to the

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:38.460
three’s company situation of their characters.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:44.130
It’s almost as if Mary will be marrying
watson and sherlock.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.630
Or marrying watson and gaining a sherlock.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:50.240
Later in the episode when watson tries to
rip the beard off a patient it’s also a

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.660
reference to the holmes character in the novels.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:57.740
The titles of the videos he tries to give
martin freeman are the same titles of the

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:01.660
books the conan doyle character tried to sell
that watson while in disguise.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.229
15 - The headbutt.

00:07:03.229 --> 00:07:07.150
Watson attacks sherlock with a headbutt in
one of the progressively dirtier restaurants

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.760
they get thrown out of.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:12.480
In the original story, watson fainted when
holmes reappeared.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:16.930
16 - Mary is a Liar - Sherlock deduces mary
and sees that she’s a liar.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:21.669
There’s a lot of theories, but most of this
will tie in with episode 2 the sign of three.

00:07:21.669 --> 00:07:28.320
When you see the date code on mary’s cypher
it’s may 11th, 2013.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:31.430
And she says that her and watson’s wedding
is in may and she refers to a possible murder.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.710
Since there’s a murder teased during the
trailer for episode 2, it means that she’s

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:34.160
probably tied up in the larger plot with the
villain this season charles augustus magnussen.

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:37.070
That doesn’t necessarily make her evil though.

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:38.810
17 - London Is Cesspool.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:43.110
Sherlock’s voice over speech london is a
cespool is something the watson wrote during

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:45.990
the original book story a study in scarlet.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.320
18 - Doctor Who references.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:51.729
Notice the round things on the wallpaper of
mr shilcot’s apartment.

00:07:51.729 --> 00:07:54.830
Inspired by the round things of the tardis
interior.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:58.660
The code name of sherlock and mycroft’s
plan to fake his death was lazarus, which

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:02.449
was an episode of doctor who that mark gatiss
both wrote and starred in.

00:08:02.449 --> 00:08:06.330
And there’s a tardis on the wall of anderson’s
apartment.

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:09.000
19 - Remember remember the fifth of november.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:15.580
It’s guy fawkes day, who is remembered for
the gunpowder plot of 1605, which the tube

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:17.510
bomb plot pays homage to.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:18.910
20 - Sherlock’s parents.

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:22.080
A lot of people recognized that sherlock’s
parents are benedict cumberbatch’s parents

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.600
in real life.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.430
But if you notice the collar on his mother’s
coat is turned up you’ll be pleased to learn

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:30.689
that his trademark upturned collars are something
he picked up from his mother.

00:08:30.689 --> 00:08:33.169
Sherlock holmes, what a mama’s boy.

00:08:33.169 --> 00:08:35.490
21 - The final explanation.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:39.020
Mark Gatiss explained that even though this
wasn’t completely correct, it was the most

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:42.330
plausible explanation as to how sherlock survived.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.570
Since I’m sure there were a ton of lines
lifted from the books and other references

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:48.200
I missed write them in the comments if you
noticed anything.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:52.880
I’ll be posting my episode 2 review tomorrow
after the episode airs.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.050
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:09:00.130
Just like last time I’ll be looking through
the comments on that video to include in my

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:07.060
episode 2 q and a video on monday. and then
a couple days after that I’ll do a new breakdown.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:10.940
Right now click here for my episode 1 q and
a and click here for my review of the episode.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.029
